<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title></title>
</head>
<body><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px">Currently, several examples can already be found in the Netherlands. Both universities of applied sciences and research universities offer transdisciplinary courses. A few examples of transdisciplinary education:</p><ul class="list-loose"><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px">In the minor <a href="https://www.avans.nl/international/studying/programmes/act-for-change-together/exchange/introduction" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Act for Change Together</a> at Avans University o f Applied Sciences, students from various disciplines collaborate with stakeholders on societal issues related to the new economy.</li></ul><ul><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px">At NHL Stenden University of Applied Sciences, students can participate in the <a href="https://www.nhlstenden.com/projecten/social-innovation-lab" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Social Innovation Lab</a> project, located in the heart of a neighborhood, where they work directly with residents to apply their practice collaboratively.</li></ul><ul><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px">In the master's insert <a href="https://www.utwente.nl/en/education/master/programmes/transdisciplinary-master-insert/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Shaping Responsible Futures</a> at the University of Twente, students work together with municipalities, NGOs, or companies on issues concerning responsible futures and systemic change.</li></ul><ul><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px">In the elective course <a href="https://placemakingamsterdam.nl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Placemaking</a> at the University of Amsterdam, students from different backgrounds engage with local residents and stakeholders to tackle urban challenges and co-create solutions.</li></ul></body>
</html>